:HELP NAME=ADDBNDDIRE.Add Binding Directory Entry (ADDBNDDIRE)
:P.Use the Add Binding Directory Entry (ADDBNDDIRE) command to add
module and service program entries to a binding directory.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDBNDDIRE/BNDDIR'.Binding directory (BNDDIR)
:P.The binding directories the binder searches for modules and service
programs to resolve imports.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDBNDDIRE/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRVPGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the service program.
:PT.:PK.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the module.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDBNDDIRE/POSITION'.Position (POSITION)
:P.The position for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PK.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Relative position
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*AFTER:EPK.
:PD.After the reference entry.
:PT.:PK.*BEFORE:EPK.
:PD.Before the reference entry.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Reference object
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Reference object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRVPGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the service program.
:PT.:PK.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the module.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGCMD.Change Command (CHGCMD)
:P.Use the Change Command (CHGCMD) command to change the attributes of a
command that the definition source does not fix.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCMD/CMD'.Command (CMD)
:P.The command for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
