:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTBNDCL.Create Bound CL Program (CRTBNDCL)
:P.Use the Create Bound CL Program (CRTBNDCL) command to compile CL
source and bind it into an ILE program in one step.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QCLSRC is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the program.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/SRCSTMF'.Source stream file (SRCSTMF)
:P.The path of the stream file that holds the source. When it is given,
SRCFILE and SRCMBR are not used.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCMBRTXT:EPK.
:PD.The text of the source member.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/DFTACTGRP'.Default activation group (DFTACTGRP)
:P.Whether to default activation group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/ACTGRP'.Activation group (ACTGRP)
:P.The activation group the program runs in&colon. a named one, a new
one each call, or the caller's.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*CALLER:EPK.
:PD.The activation group of the caller.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STGMDL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/STGMDL'.Storage model (STGMDL)
:P.The storage model of the program's automatic and static
storage&colon. single-level, teraspace, or inherited from the activation
group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SNGLVL:EPK.
:PD.Single-level storage.
:PT.:PK.*TERASPACE:EPK.
:PD.Teraspace storage.
:PT.:PK.*INHERIT:EPK.
:PD.Inherited from the activation group.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/OPTION'.Source listing options (OPTION)
:P.The source listing options for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PK.*NOGEN:EPK.
:PD.The object is not created; only the listing is.
:PT.:PK.*XREF:EPK.
:PD.With a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOXREF:EPK.
:PD.Without a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*NOSECLVL:EPK.
:PD.Without the second-level text of the messages.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *EVENTF, *NOEVENTF.
:P.When no value is given, *GEN *NOXREF *NOSECLVL *NOEVENTF is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/LOG'.Log commands (LOG)
:P.The log commands for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/ALWRTVSRC'.Allow RTVCLSRC (ALWRTVSRC)
:P.Whether RTVCLSRC can retrieve the source from the program.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/REPLACE'.Replace program (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/TGTRLS'.Target release (TGTRLS)
:P.The release of the operating system the object is created for.
*CURRENT is this release; *PRV is the previous one.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.This release.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/LANGID'.Language ID (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/INCFILE'.Include file (INCFILE)
:P.The source file that /COPY and /INCLUDE directives without a file
name search.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCFILE:EPK.
:PD.The source file of the object.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/OPTIMIZE'.Optimize (OPTIMIZE)
:P.The level of optimization the code generator applies. Higher levels
run faster but are harder to debug.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/DBGVIEW'.Debugging view (DBGVIEW)
:P.The debug view kept in the object&colon. none, the statements, the
source, a listing, or all of them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STMT:EPK.
:PD.The statement view.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/DBGENCKEY'.Debug encryption key (DBGENCKEY)
:P.A key that protects the debug view stored in the object; the same key
must be given to debug it.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 16 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/ENBPFRCOL'.Performance collection (ENBPFRCOL)
:P.Whether the program collects performance data, and at which procedure
entries and exits.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PEP, *ENTRYEXIT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDCL/BNDDIR'.Binding directory (BNDDIR)
:P.The binding directories the binder searches for modules and service
programs to resolve imports.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTBNDDIR.Create Binding Directory (CRTBNDDIR)
:P.Use the Create Binding Directory (CRTBNDDIR) command to create an
empty binding directory.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDDIR/BNDDIR'.Binding directory (BNDDIR)
:P.The binding directories the binder searches for modules and service
programs to resolve imports.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDDIR/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDDIR/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTBNDRPG.Create Bound RPG Program (CRTBNDRPG)
:P.Use the Create Bound RPG Program (CRTBNDRPG) command to compile ILE
RPG source and bind it into a program in one step.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CTLSPEC.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QRPGLESRC is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the program.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/SRCSTMF'.Source stream file (SRCSTMF)
:P.The path of the stream file that holds the source. When it is given,
SRCFILE and SRCMBR are not used.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/GENLVL'.Severity that stops creation (GENLVL)
:P.The severity of the compile messages at or above which the object is
not created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 2 digits. The value must be from 0 to 20.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 10 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCMBRTXT:EPK.
:PD.The text of the source member.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/DFTACTGRP'.Default activation group (DFTACTGRP)
:P.Whether to default activation group.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/ACTGRP'.Activation group (ACTGRP)
:P.The activation group the program runs in&colon. a named one, a new
one each call, or the caller's.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*CALLER:EPK.
:PD.The activation group of the caller.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STGMDL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/STGMDL'.Storage model (STGMDL)
:P.The storage model of the program's automatic and static
storage&colon. single-level, teraspace, or inherited from the activation
group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SNGLVL:EPK.
:PD.Single-level storage.
:PT.:PK.*TERASPACE:EPK.
:PD.Teraspace storage.
:PT.:PK.*INHERIT:EPK.
:PD.Inherited from the activation group.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/OPTION'.Compile options (OPTION)
:P.The compile options for this command.
:P.Up to 12 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*XREF:EPK.
:PD.With a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOXREF:EPK.
:PD.Without a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PK.*NOGEN:EPK.
:PD.The object is not created; only the listing is.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*NOSECLVL:EPK.
:PD.Without the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*EXT:EPK.
:PD.Extended.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SHOWCPY, *NOSHOWCPY, *EXPDDS, *NOEXPDDS,
*NOEXT, *SHOWSKP, *NOSHOWSKP, *SRCSTMT, *NOSRCSTMT, *DEBUGIO,
*NODEBUGIO, *UNREF, *NOUNREF, *EVENTF, *NOEVENTF.
:P.When no value is given, *XREF *GEN *NOSECLVL *SHOWCPY *EXPDDS *EXT
*NOSHOWSKP *NOSRCSTMT *DEBUGIO *NOEVENTF is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/DBGVIEW'.Debugging view (DBGVIEW)
:P.The debug view kept in the object&colon. none, the statements, the
source, a listing, or all of them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STMT:EPK.
:PD.The statement view.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:PT.:PK.*COPY:EPK.
:PD.A copy.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/DBGENCKEY'.Debug encryption key (DBGENCKEY)
:P.A key that protects the debug view stored in the object; the same key
must be given to debug it.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 16 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/OUTPUT'.Listing (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/OPTIMIZE'.Optimize (OPTIMIZE)
:P.The level of optimization the code generator applies. Higher levels
run faster but are harder to debug.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/INDENT'.Listing nesting mark (INDENT)
:P.The listing nesting mark for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/CVTOPT'.External types to convert (CVTOPT)
:P.The external types to convert for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DATETIME, *NODATETIME, *GRAPHIC, *NOGRAPHIC,
*VARCHAR, *NOVARCHAR, *VARGRAPHIC, *NOVARGRAPHIC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/LANGID'.Language ID (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/REPLACE'.Replace program (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/USRPRF'.Run under profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/TRUNCNBR'.Truncate numbers that overflow (TRUNCNBR)
:P.Whether to truncate numbers that overflow.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/FIXNBR'.Repair bad decimal data (FIXNBR)
:P.The repair bad decimal data for this command.
:P.Up to 2 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ZONED, *NOZONED, *INPUTPACKED, *NOINPUTPACKED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/TGTRLS'.Target release (TGTRLS)
:P.The release of the operating system the object is created for.
*CURRENT is this release; *PRV is the previous one.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.This release.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/ALWNULL'.Null-capable fields (ALWNULL)
:P.The null-capable fields for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *INPUTONLY, *USRCTL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/DEFINE'.Condition names to define (DEFINE)
:P.The condition names to define for this command.
:P.Up to 32 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/ENBPFRCOL'.Performance collection (ENBPFRCOL)
:P.Whether the program collects performance data, and at which procedure
entries and exits.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PEP, *ENTRYEXIT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/PRFDTA'.Profiling data (PRFDTA)
:P.Whether the program collects profiling data that later optimization
can use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOCOL, *COL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/LICOPT'.Code generator options (LICOPT)
:P.The code generator options for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/INCDIR'.Include directories (INCDIR)
:P.The include directories for this command.
:P.Up to 32 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/PGMINFO'.Interface information (PGMINFO)
:P.The interface information for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Kind
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PCML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Kept in
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STMF:EPK.
:PD.A stream file.
:PT.:PK.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the module.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/INFOSTMF'.Interface stream file (INFOSTMF)
:P.The interface stream file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/PPGENOPT'.Preprocessor output options (PPGENOPT)
:P.The preprocessor output options for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RMVCOMMENT, *NORMVCOMMENT, *EXPINCLUDE,
*NOEXPINCLUDE, *NOSEQSRC, *SEQSRC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/PPSRCFILE'.Preprocessor output file (PPSRCFILE)
:P.The preprocessor output file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QSQLPRE is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QTEMP is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/PPSRCMBR'.Preprocessor output member (PPSRCMBR)
:P.The preprocessor output member for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the program.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/PPSRCSTMF'.Preprocessor stream file (PPSRCSTMF)
:P.The preprocessor stream file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SRCSTMF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/TGTCCSID'.CCSID to compile in (TGTCCSID)
:P.The CCSID to compile in for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/REQPREXP'.Prototypes for exports (REQPREXP)
:P.The prototypes for exports for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*WARN:EPK.
:PD.A warning message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REQUIRE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTBNDRPG/BNDDIR'.Binding directory (BNDDIR)
:P.The binding directories the binder searches for modules and service
programs to resolve imports.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTCLMOD.Create CL Module (CRTCLMOD)
:P.Use the Create CL Module (CRTCLMOD) command to compile CL source into
an ILE module.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/MODULE'.Module (MODULE)
:P.The modules bound into the program or service program.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QCLSRC is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the module.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/SRCSTMF'.Source stream file (SRCSTMF)
:P.The path of the stream file that holds the source. When it is given,
SRCFILE and SRCMBR are not used.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCMBRTXT:EPK.
:PD.The text of the source member.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/OPTION'.Source listing options (OPTION)
:P.The source listing options for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PK.*NOGEN:EPK.
:PD.The object is not created; only the listing is.
:PT.:PK.*XREF:EPK.
:PD.With a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOXREF:EPK.
:PD.Without a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*NOSECLVL:EPK.
:PD.Without the second-level text of the messages.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *EVENTF, *NOEVENTF.
:P.When no value is given, *GEN *NOXREF *NOSECLVL *NOEVENTF is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/OPTIMIZE'.Optimize (OPTIMIZE)
:P.The level of optimization the code generator applies. Higher levels
run faster but are harder to debug.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/DBGVIEW'.Debugging view (DBGVIEW)
:P.The debug view kept in the object&colon. none, the statements, the
source, a listing, or all of them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STMT:EPK.
:PD.The statement view.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/DBGENCKEY'.Debug encryption key (DBGENCKEY)
:P.A key that protects the debug view stored in the object; the same key
must be given to debug it.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 16 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/REPLACE'.Replace module (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/LOG'.Log commands (LOG)
:P.The log commands for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/ALWRTVSRC'.Allow RTVCLSRC (ALWRTVSRC)
:P.Whether RTVCLSRC can retrieve the source from the program.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/INCFILE'.Include file (INCFILE)
:P.The source file that /COPY and /INCLUDE directives without a file
name search.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCFILE:EPK.
:PD.The source file of the object.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/TGTRLS'.Target release (TGTRLS)
:P.The release of the operating system the object is created for.
*CURRENT is this release; *PRV is the previous one.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.This release.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/LANGID'.Language ID (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLMOD/ENBPFRCOL'.Performance collection (ENBPFRCOL)
:P.Whether the program collects performance data, and at which procedure
entries and exits.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PEP, *ENTRYEXIT.
:EHELP.
