:HELP NAME='CRTCLPGM/OPTION'.Source listing options (OPTION)
:P.The source listing options for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PK.*NOGEN:EPK.
:PD.The object is not created; only the listing is.
:PT.:PK.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*NOSRC:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOSOURCE:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*XREF:EPK.
:PD.With a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOXREF:EPK.
:PD.Without a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*NOSECLVL:EPK.
:PD.Without the second-level text of the messages.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *GEN *NOSRC *NOXREF *NOSECLVL is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLPGM/GENOPT'.Generation options (GENOPT)
:P.The generation options for this command.
:P.Up to 6 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:PT.:PK.*NOXREF:EPK.
:PD.Without a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*XREF:EPK.
:PD.With a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*OPTIMIZE:EPK.
:PD.The system chooses the best way.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOPATCH, *PATCH, *NODUMP, *DUMP, *NOATR, *ATR,
*NOOPTIMIZE.
:P.When no value is given, *NOLIST *NOXREF *NOPATCH *NODUMP *NOATR
*NOOPTIMIZE is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLPGM/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
