:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLPGM/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLPGM/LANGID'.Language ID (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLPGM/INCFILE'.Include file (INCFILE)
:P.The source file that /COPY and /INCLUDE directives without a file
name search.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCFILE:EPK.
:PD.The source file of the object.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLPGM/DBGENCKEY'.Debug encryption key (DBGENCKEY)
:P.A key that protects the debug view stored in the object; the same key
must be given to debug it.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 16 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTCMD.Create Command (CRTCMD)
:P.Use the Create Command (CRTCMD) command to compile a command
definition source into a *CMD object.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/CMD'.Command (CMD)
:P.The command for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/PGM'.Program to process command (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REXX.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QCMDSRC is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CMD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the command.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/SRCSTMF'.Source stream file (SRCSTMF)
:P.The path of the stream file that holds the source. When it is given,
SRCFILE and SRCMBR are not used.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/REXSRCFILE'.REXX source file (REXSRCFILE)
:P.The REXX source file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QREXSRC is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/REXSRCMBR'.REXX source member (REXSRCMBR)
:P.The REXX source member for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CMD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the command.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/REXCMDENV'.REXX command environment (REXCMDENV)
:P.The REXX command environment for this command.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *COMMAND, *CPICOMM, *EXECSQL.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/THDSAFE'.Threadsafe (THDSAFE)
:P.The threadsafe for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *COND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/MLTTHDACN'.Multithreaded job action (MLTTHDACN)
:P.The multithreaded job action for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RUN, *NORUN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCMBRTXT:EPK.
:PD.The text of the source member.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/VLDCKR'.Validity checking program (VLDCKR)
:P.The validity checking program for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/MODE'.Mode in which valid (MODE)
:P.The mode in which valid for this command.
:P.Up to 3 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*SERVICE:EPK.
:PD.Service.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PROD, *DEBUG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/ALLOW'.Where allowed to run (ALLOW)
:P.The where allowed to run for this command.
:P.Up to 9 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*BATCH:EPK.
:PD.Batch jobs.
:PT.:PK.*INTERACT:EPK.
:PD.Interactive jobs.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BPGM, *IPGM, *BREXX, *IREXX, *EXEC, *BMOD,
*IMOD.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/ALWLMTUSR'.Allow limited users (ALWLMTUSR)
:P.Whether to allow limited users.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/MAXPOS'.Max positional parameters (MAXPOS)
:P.The max positional parameters for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/PMTFILE'.Prompt file (PMTFILE)
:P.The prompt file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. File
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Message retrieval
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STATIC, *DYNAMIC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/MSGF'.Message file (MSGF)
:P.The message file that holds the message descriptions, by name and
library.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QCPFMSG is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/HLPPNLGRP'.Help panel group (HLPPNLGRP)
:P.The help panel group for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/HLPID'.Help identifier (HLPID)
:P.The help identifier for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*CMD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the command.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/HLPSCHIDX'.Help search index (HLPSCHIDX)
:P.The help search index for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/CURLIB'.Current library (CURLIB)
:P.The current library of the job&colon. the library searched first by
name (after the system part of the library list) and where *CURLIB puts
new objects.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOCHG:EPK.
:PD.Not changed.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CRTDFT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/PRDLIB'.Product library (PRDLIB)
:P.The product library of the command&colon. it is added to the library
list while the command runs.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOCHG:EPK.
:PD.Not changed.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/PMTOVRPGM'.Prompt override program (PMTOVRPGM)
:P.The prompt override program for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/ENBGUI'.Enable GUI (ENBGUI)
:P.Whether to enable GUI.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCMD/REPLACE'.Replace command (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTPGM.Create Program (CRTPGM)
:P.Use the Create Program (CRTPGM) command to bind modules and service
programs into an ILE program.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/MODULE'.Module (MODULE)
:P.The modules bound into the program or service program.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the program.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/ENTMOD'.Program entry module (ENTMOD)
:P.The program entry module for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the program.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/BNDSRVPGM'.Bind service program (BNDSRVPGM)
:P.The service programs bound by reference to the program.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Service program
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Activation
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*DEFER:EPK.
:PD.Later, when it is needed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/BNDDIR'.Binding directory (BNDDIR)
:P.The binding directories the binder searches for modules and service
programs to resolve imports.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/ACTGRP'.Activation group (ACTGRP)
:P.The activation group the program runs in&colon. a named one, a new
one each call, or the caller's.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*CALLER:EPK.
:PD.The activation group of the caller.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/OPTION'.Creation options (OPTION)
:P.The creation options for this command.
:P.Up to 5 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PK.*NOGEN:EPK.
:PD.The object is not created; only the listing is.
:PT.:PK.*WARN:EPK.
:PD.A warning message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NODUPPROC, *DUPPROC, *NODUPVAR, *DUPVAR,
*NOWARN, *RSLVREF, *UNRSLVREF.
:P.When no value is given, *GEN *NODUPPROC *NODUPVAR *WARN *RSLVREF is
used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/DETAIL'.Listing detail (DETAIL)
:P.The listing detail for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*EXTENDED:EPK.
:PD.Extended detail.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/ALWUPD'.Allow update (ALWUPD)
:P.Whether records can be updated through this file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/ALWLIBUPD'.Allow bound *SRVPGM lib update (ALWLIBUPD)
:P.Whether UPDPGM and UPDSRVPGM may change the library of a bound
service program.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/REPLACE'.Replace program (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ENTMODTXT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/TGTRLS'.Target release (TGTRLS)
:P.The release of the operating system the object is created for.
*CURRENT is this release; *PRV is the previous one.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.This release.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/ALWRINZ'.Allow reinitialization (ALWRINZ)
:P.Whether the program's static storage may be reinitialized while it is
active.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/STGMDL'.Storage model (STGMDL)
:P.The storage model of the program's automatic and static
storage&colon. single-level, teraspace, or inherited from the activation
group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SNGLVL:EPK.
:PD.Single-level storage.
:PT.:PK.*TERASPACE:EPK.
:PD.Teraspace storage.
:PT.:PK.*INHERIT:EPK.
:PD.Inherited from the activation group.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/IPA'.Interprocedural analysis (IPA)
:P.Whether to interprocedural analysis.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/IPACTLFILE'.IPA control file (IPACTLFILE)
:P.The IPA control file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/ARGOPT'.Argument optimization (ARGOPT)
:P.Whether argument passing is optimized for the program's procedure
calls.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPGM/PRFDTA'.Profiling data (PRFDTA)
:P.Whether the program collects profiling data that later optimization
can use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOCOL, *COL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTPRXCMD.Create Proxy Command (CRTPRXCMD)
:P.Use the Create Proxy Command (CRTPRXCMD) command to create a proxy
command that stands for another command.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRXCMD/CMD'.Proxy command (CMD)
:P.The proxy command for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRXCMD/TGTCMD'.Target command (TGTCMD)
:P.The target command for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRXCMD/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRXCMD/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPRXCMD/REPLACE'.Replace command (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTRPGMOD.Create RPG Module (CRTRPGMOD)
:P.Use the Create RPG Module (CRTRPGMOD) command to compile ILE RPG
source into a module.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/MODULE'.Module (MODULE)
:P.The modules bound into the program or service program.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CTLSPEC.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QRPGLESRC is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the module.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/SRCSTMF'.Source stream file (SRCSTMF)
:P.The path of the stream file that holds the source. When it is given,
SRCFILE and SRCMBR are not used.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/GENLVL'.Severity that stops creation (GENLVL)
:P.The severity of the compile messages at or above which the object is
not created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 2 digits. The value must be from 0 to 20.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 10 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCMBRTXT:EPK.
:PD.The text of the source member.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/OUTPUT'.Listing (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/OPTION'.Compile options (OPTION)
:P.The compile options for this command.
:P.Up to 12 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*XREF:EPK.
:PD.With a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOXREF:EPK.
:PD.Without a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PK.*NOGEN:EPK.
:PD.The object is not created; only the listing is.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*NOSECLVL:EPK.
:PD.Without the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*EXT:EPK.
:PD.Extended.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SHOWCPY, *NOSHOWCPY, *EXPDDS, *NOEXPDDS,
*NOEXT, *SHOWSKP, *NOSHOWSKP, *SRCSTMT, *NOSRCSTMT, *DEBUGIO,
*NODEBUGIO, *UNREF, *NOUNREF, *EVENTF, *NOEVENTF.
:P.When no value is given, *XREF *GEN *NOSECLVL *SHOWCPY *EXPDDS *EXT
*NOSHOWSKP *NOSRCSTMT *DEBUGIO *NOEVENTF is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/DBGVIEW'.Debugging view (DBGVIEW)
:P.The debug view kept in the object&colon. none, the statements, the
source, a listing, or all of them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STMT:EPK.
:PD.The statement view.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:PT.:PK.*COPY:EPK.
:PD.A copy.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/DBGENCKEY'.Debug encryption key (DBGENCKEY)
:P.A key that protects the debug view stored in the object; the same key
must be given to debug it.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 16 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/OPTIMIZE'.Optimize (OPTIMIZE)
:P.The level of optimization the code generator applies. Higher levels
run faster but are harder to debug.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/INDENT'.Listing nesting mark (INDENT)
:P.The listing nesting mark for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/CVTOPT'.External types to convert (CVTOPT)
:P.The external types to convert for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DATETIME, *NODATETIME, *GRAPHIC, *NOGRAPHIC,
*VARCHAR, *NOVARCHAR, *VARGRAPHIC, *NOVARGRAPHIC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/LANGID'.Language ID (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/REPLACE'.Replace module (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/TRUNCNBR'.Truncate numbers that overflow (TRUNCNBR)
:P.Whether to truncate numbers that overflow.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/FIXNBR'.Repair bad decimal data (FIXNBR)
:P.The repair bad decimal data for this command.
:P.Up to 2 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ZONED, *NOZONED, *INPUTPACKED, *NOINPUTPACKED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/TGTRLS'.Target release (TGTRLS)
:P.The release of the operating system the object is created for.
*CURRENT is this release; *PRV is the previous one.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.This release.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/ALWNULL'.Null-capable fields (ALWNULL)
:P.The null-capable fields for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *INPUTONLY, *USRCTL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/DEFINE'.Condition names to define (DEFINE)
:P.The condition names to define for this command.
:P.Up to 32 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/ENBPFRCOL'.Performance collection (ENBPFRCOL)
:P.Whether the program collects performance data, and at which procedure
entries and exits.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PEP, *ENTRYEXIT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/STGMDL'.Storage model (STGMDL)
:P.The storage model of the program's automatic and static
storage&colon. single-level, teraspace, or inherited from the activation
group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SNGLVL:EPK.
:PD.Single-level storage.
:PT.:PK.*TERASPACE:EPK.
:PD.Teraspace storage.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INHERIT:EPK.
:PD.Inherited from the activation group.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/BNDDIR'.Binding directory (BNDDIR)
:P.The binding directories the binder searches for modules and service
programs to resolve imports.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/PRFDTA'.Profiling data (PRFDTA)
:P.Whether the program collects profiling data that later optimization
can use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOCOL, *COL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/LICOPT'.Code generator options (LICOPT)
:P.The code generator options for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/INCDIR'.Include directories (INCDIR)
:P.The include directories for this command.
:P.Up to 32 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/PGMINFO'.Interface information (PGMINFO)
:P.The interface information for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Kind
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PCML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Kept in
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STMF:EPK.
:PD.A stream file.
:PT.:PK.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the module.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/INFOSTMF'.Interface stream file (INFOSTMF)
:P.The interface stream file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/PPGENOPT'.Preprocessor output options (PPGENOPT)
:P.The preprocessor output options for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RMVCOMMENT, *NORMVCOMMENT, *EXPINCLUDE,
*NOEXPINCLUDE, *NOSEQSRC, *SEQSRC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/PPSRCFILE'.Preprocessor output file (PPSRCFILE)
:P.The preprocessor output file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QSQLPRE is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QTEMP is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/PPSRCMBR'.Preprocessor output member (PPSRCMBR)
:P.The preprocessor output member for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the module.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/PPSRCSTMF'.Preprocessor stream file (PPSRCSTMF)
:P.The preprocessor stream file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SRCSTMF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/TGTCCSID'.CCSID to compile in (TGTCCSID)
:P.The CCSID to compile in for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGMOD/REQPREXP'.Prototypes for exports (REQPREXP)
:P.The prototypes for exports for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*WARN:EPK.
:PD.A warning message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REQUIRE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTRPGPGM.Create RPG/400 Program (CRTRPGPGM)
:P.Use the Create RPG/400 Program (CRTRPGPGM) command to compile RPG III
(RPG/400) source into a program (licensed program QS00RPG,
docs/RPG3.md).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CTLSPEC.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QRPGSRC is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the program.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/GENLVL'.Generation severity level (GENLVL)
:P.The severity of the compile messages at or above which the object is
not created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 2 digits. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 9 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCMBRTXT:EPK.
:PD.The text of the source member.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/OPTION'.Source listing options (OPTION)
:P.The source listing options for this command.
:P.Up to 7 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*NOSOURCE:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*NOSRC:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*XREF:EPK.
:PD.With a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOXREF:EPK.
:PD.Without a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PK.*NOGEN:EPK.
:PD.The object is not created; only the listing is.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*NOSECLVL:EPK.
:PD.Without the second-level text of the messages.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DUMP, *NODUMP, *SRCDBG, *NOSRCDBG, *LSTDBG,
*NOLSTDBG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/GENOPT'.Generation options (GENOPT)
:P.The generation options for this command.
:P.Up to 7 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:PT.:PK.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:PT.:PK.*XREF:EPK.
:PD.With a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOXREF:EPK.
:PD.Without a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*OPTIMIZE:EPK.
:PD.The system chooses the best way.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ATR, *NOATR, *DUMP, *NODUMP, *PATCH, *NOPATCH,
*NOOPTIMIZE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/INDENT'.Source listing indentation (INDENT)
:P.The source listing indentation for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/CVTOPT'.Type conversion options (CVTOPT)
:P.The type conversion options for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DATETIME, *NODATETIME, *VARCHAR, *NOVARCHAR,
*GRAPHIC, *NOGRAPHIC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/LANGID'.Language identifier (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/SAAFLAG'.SAA flagging (SAAFLAG)
:P.Whether the listing marks statements that are not part of the IBM SQL
language standard.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOFLAG, *FLAG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/PRTFILE'.Print file (PRTFILE)
:P.The printer file the printed output is written with, by name and
library.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QSYSPRT is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/REPLACE'.Replace program (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/TGTRLS'.Target release (TGTRLS)
:P.The release of the operating system the object is created for.
*CURRENT is this release; *PRV is the previous one.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.This release.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/PHSTRC'.Phase trace (PHSTRC)
:P.Whether to phase trace.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/ITDUMP'.Intermediate text dump (ITDUMP)
:P.The intermediate text dump for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/SNPDUMP'.Snap dump (SNPDUMP)
:P.The snap dump for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/CODELIST'.Codelist (CODELIST)
:P.The codelist for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/IGNDECERR'.Ignore decimal data error (IGNDECERR)
:P.Whether to ignore decimal data error.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTRPGPGM/ALWNULL'.Allow null values (ALWNULL)
:P.Whether to allow null values.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTSQLRPGI.Create SQL ILE RPG Object (CRTSQLRPGI)
:P.Use the Create SQL ILE RPG Object (CRTSQLRPGI) command to precompile
ILE RPG source with embedded SQL, then make a program, a service program
or a module of it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QRPGLESRC is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/SRCSTMF'.Source stream file (SRCSTMF)
:P.The path of the stream file that holds the source. When it is given,
SRCFILE and SRCMBR are not used.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/COMMIT'.Commitment control (COMMIT)
:P.The commitment control level&colon. whether changes are made in units
the program commits or rolls back, and which records are locked.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CHG:EPK.
:PD.Changed records are locked until committed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*CS:EPK.
:PD.Cursor stability.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*RR:EPK.
:PD.Repeatable read.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *UR, *RS, *NC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/RDB'.Relational database (RDB)
:P.The relational database for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOCAL:EPK.
:PD.This system.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 18 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/OBJTYPE'.Compile type (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the program.
:PT.:PK.*SRVPGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the service program.
:PT.:PK.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the module.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/OUTPUT'.Listing output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCMBRTXT:EPK.
:PD.The text of the source member.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/OPTION'.Precompiler options (OPTION)
:P.The precompiler options for this command.
:P.Up to 12 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*XREF:EPK.
:PD.With a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOXREF:EPK.
:PD.Without a cross-reference listing.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PK.*NOGEN:EPK.
:PD.The object is not created; only the listing is.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*NOSECLVL:EPK.
:PD.Without the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*SYS:EPK.
:PD.The system's value.
:PT.:PK.*SQL:EPK.
:PD.SQL.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*PERIOD:EPK.
:PD.A period.
:PT.:PK.*COMMA:EPK.
:PD.A comma.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CVTDT, *NOCVTDT, *EVENTF, *NOEVENTF, *EXTIND,
*NOEXTIND, *NOLSTDBG, *LSTDBG.
:P.When no value is given, *XREF *GEN *NOSECLVL *SYS *JOB *NOCVTDT
*NOEVENTF *NOEXTIND is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/RPGPPOPT'.RPG preprocessor options (RPGPPOPT)
:P.Whether the RPG compiler's preprocessor runs over the source
(expanding /COPY and /INCLUDE and the conditional directives) before the
SQL precompile reads it.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LVL1, *LVL2.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/TGTRLS'.Target release (TGTRLS)
:P.The release of the operating system the object is created for.
*CURRENT is this release; *PRV is the previous one.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.This release.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/INCFILE'.INCLUDE file (INCFILE)
:P.The source file that /COPY and /INCLUDE directives without a file
name search.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCFILE:EPK.
:PD.The source file of the object.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/INCDIR'.SQL INCLUDE directory (INCDIR)
:P.The SQL INCLUDE directory for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/ALWCPYDTA'.Allow copy of data (ALWCPYDTA)
:P.Whether a copy of the data may be used to answer a query.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*OPTIMIZE:EPK.
:PD.The system chooses the best way.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/CLOSQLCSR'.Close SQL cursor (CLOSQLCSR)
:P.When the SQL cursors the program opens are closed and its prepared
statements discarded&colon. when the module ends or when the activation
group ends.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ENDACTGRP, *ENDMOD.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/ALWBLK'.Allow blocking (ALWBLK)
:P.The allow blocking for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*READ:EPK.
:PD.Read authority.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLREAD.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/DLYPRP'.Delay PREPARE (DLYPRP)
:P.Whether to delay PREPARE.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/CONACC'.Concurrent access resolution (CONACC)
:P.What a statement does when a row it reads is locked by another job's
uncommitted change&colon. the default for the isolation level, use the
currently committed value, or wait for the lock.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CURCMT, *WAIT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/GENLVL'.Severity level (GENLVL)
:P.The severity of the compile messages at or above which the object is
not created.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 2 digits. The value must be from 0 to 40.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 10 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/DATFMT'.Date format (DATFMT)
:P.The format of dates&colon. the order of year, month and day.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*USA:EPK.
:PD.The USA format, mm/dd/yyyy or hh&colon.mm AM.
:PT.:PK.*ISO:EPK.
:PD.The ISO format, yyyy-mm-dd or hh.mm.ss.
:PT.:PK.*EUR:EPK.
:PD.The European format, dd.mm.yyyy or hh.mm.ss.
:PT.:PK.*JIS:EPK.
:PD.The Japanese industrial standard format, yyyy-mm-dd or
hh&colon.mm&colon.ss.
:PT.:PK.*MDY:EPK.
:PD.Month, day, year.
:PT.:PK.*DMY:EPK.
:PD.Day, month, year.
:PT.:PK.*YMD:EPK.
:PD.Year, month, day.
:PT.:PK.*JUL:EPK.
:PD.Julian&colon. year and day of the year.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/DATSEP'.Date separator character (DATSEP)
:P.The character between the parts of a date.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/TIMFMT'.Time format (TIMFMT)
:P.The format of times.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*HMS:EPK.
:PD.Hours, minutes and seconds.
:PT.:PK.*USA:EPK.
:PD.The USA format, mm/dd/yyyy or hh&colon.mm AM.
:PT.:PK.*ISO:EPK.
:PD.The ISO format, yyyy-mm-dd or hh.mm.ss.
:PT.:PK.*EUR:EPK.
:PD.The European format, dd.mm.yyyy or hh.mm.ss.
:PT.:PK.*JIS:EPK.
:PD.The Japanese industrial standard format, yyyy-mm-dd or
hh&colon.mm&colon.ss.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/TIMSEP'.Time separator character (TIMSEP)
:P.The character between the parts of a time.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/REPLACE'.Replace (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/RDBCNNMTH'.RDB connect method (RDBCNNMTH)
:P.The RDB connect method for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DUW, *RUW.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/DFTRDBCOL'.Default collection (DFTRDBCOL)
:P.The schema used for unqualified names in SQL statements with system
naming.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/DYNDFTCOL'.Dynamic default collection (DYNDFTCOL)
:P.Whether to dynamic default collection.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/SQLPKG'.Package (SQLPKG)
:P.The package for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJLIB.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/SQLPATH'.SQL path (SQLPATH)
:P.The SQL path for this command.
:P.Up to 268 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NAMING.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/SQLCURRULE'.SQL rules (SQLCURRULE)
:P.Whether DB2 or the standard SQL rules apply to the program's
statements.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DB2.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/SAAFLAG'.IBM SQL flagging (SAAFLAG)
:P.Whether the listing marks statements that are not part of the IBM SQL
language standard.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOFLAG, *FLAG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/FLAGSTD'.ANS flagging (FLAGSTD)
:P.Whether the listing marks statements that do not conform to the ANSI
SQL standard.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ANS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/PRTFILE'.Print file (PRTFILE)
:P.The printer file the printed output is written with, by name and
library.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QSYSPRT is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/DBGVIEW'.Debugging view (DBGVIEW)
:P.The debug view kept in the object&colon. none, the statements, the
source, a listing, or all of them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*STMT:EPK.
:PD.The statement view.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/DBGENCKEY'.Debug encryption key (DBGENCKEY)
:P.A key that protects the debug view stored in the object; the same key
must be given to debug it.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 16 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NAMING.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/DYNUSRPRF'.Dynamic user profile (DYNUSRPRF)
:P.The user profile dynamic SQL statements run under&colon. the user's,
or the program owner's.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/LANGID'.Language id (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*JOBRUN:EPK.
:PD.The value used while the job runs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/CVTCCSID'.Conversion CCSID (CVTCCSID)
:P.The conversion CCSID for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/TOSRCFILE'.To source file (TOSRCFILE)
:P.The to source file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QTEMP is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/DECRESULT'.Decimal result options (DECRESULT)
:P.The precision and scale of decimal results the program's SQL
statements compute.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Maximum precision
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 31 to 63.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 31 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Maximum scale
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 31 to 63.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 31 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Minimum divide scale
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 9.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/DECFLTRND'.Decimal float rounding mode (DECFLTRND)
:P.How DECFLOAT results are rounded when they have more digits than the
type holds.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *HALFEVEN, *UP, *DOWN, *CEILING, *FLOOR,
*HALFUP, *HALFDOWN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSQLRPGI/COMPILEOPT'.Compiler options (COMPILEOPT)
:P.The compiler options for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTSRVPGM.Create Service Program (CRTSRVPGM)
:P.Use the Create Service Program (CRTSRVPGM) command to bind modules
into a service program with an export list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/SRVPGM'.Service program (SRVPGM)
:P.The service program, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/MODULE'.Module (MODULE)
:P.The modules bound into the program or service program.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRVPGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the service program.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/EXPORT'.Export (EXPORT)
:P.The export for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCFILE:EPK.
:PD.The source file of the object.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/SRCFILE'.Export source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QSRVSRC is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/SRCMBR'.Export source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRVPGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the service program.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/SRCSTMF'.Export source stream file (SRCSTMF)
:P.The path of the stream file that holds the source. When it is given,
SRCFILE and SRCMBR are not used.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/BNDSRVPGM'.Bind service program (BNDSRVPGM)
:P.The service programs bound by reference to the program.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Service program
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Activation
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*DEFER:EPK.
:PD.Later, when it is needed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/BNDDIR'.Binding directory (BNDDIR)
:P.The binding directories the binder searches for modules and service
programs to resolve imports.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/ACTGRP'.Activation group (ACTGRP)
:P.The activation group the program runs in&colon. a named one, a new
one each call, or the caller's.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALLER:EPK.
:PD.The activation group of the caller.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/OPTION'.Creation options (OPTION)
:P.The creation options for this command.
:P.Up to 5 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PK.*NOGEN:EPK.
:PD.The object is not created; only the listing is.
:PT.:PK.*WARN:EPK.
:PD.A warning message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NODUPPROC, *DUPPROC, *NODUPVAR, *DUPVAR,
*NOWARN, *RSLVREF, *UNRSLVREF.
:P.When no value is given, *GEN *NODUPPROC *NODUPVAR *WARN *RSLVREF is
used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/DETAIL'.Listing detail (DETAIL)
:P.The listing detail for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*EXTENDED:EPK.
:PD.Extended detail.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/ALWUPD'.Allow update (ALWUPD)
:P.Whether records can be updated through this file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/ALWLIBUPD'.Allow bound *SRVPGM lib update (ALWLIBUPD)
:P.Whether UPDPGM and UPDSRVPGM may change the library of a bound
service program.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/REPLACE'.Replace service program (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/TGTRLS'.Target release (TGTRLS)
:P.The release of the operating system the object is created for.
*CURRENT is this release; *PRV is the previous one.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.This release.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/ALWRINZ'.Allow reinitialization (ALWRINZ)
:P.Whether the program's static storage may be reinitialized while it is
active.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/STGMDL'.Storage model (STGMDL)
:P.The storage model of the program's automatic and static
storage&colon. single-level, teraspace, or inherited from the activation
group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SNGLVL:EPK.
:PD.Single-level storage.
:PT.:PK.*TERASPACE:EPK.
:PD.Teraspace storage.
:PT.:PK.*INHERIT:EPK.
:PD.Inherited from the activation group.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/IPA'.Interprocedural analysis (IPA)
:P.Whether to interprocedural analysis.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/IPACTLFILE'.IPA control file (IPACTLFILE)
:P.The IPA control file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/ARGOPT'.Argument optimization (ARGOPT)
:P.Whether argument passing is optimized for the program's procedure
calls.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSRVPGM/PRFDTA'.Profiling data (PRFDTA)
:P.Whether the program collects profiling data that later optimization
can use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOCOL, *COL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CVTRPGSRC.Convert RPG Source (CVTRPGSRC)
:P.Use the Convert RPG Source (CVTRPGSRC) command to convert RPG III
source members to ILE RPG (licensed program QS00RPG, docs/RPG3.md).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CVTRPGSRC/FROMFILE'.From file (FROMFILE)
:P.The file the data comes from.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CVTRPGSRC/FROMMBR'.From member (FROMMBR)
:P.The member the data comes from.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CVTRPGSRC/TOFILE'.To file (TOFILE)
:P.The file that receives the data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QRPGLESRC is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CVTRPGSRC/TOMBR'.To member (TOMBR)
:P.The member of the to-file that receives the data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FROMMBR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CVTRPGSRC/EXPCPY'.Expand copy member (EXPCPY)
:P.Whether to expand copy member.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CVTRPGSRC/CVTRPT'.Print conversion report (CVTRPT)
:P.Whether to print conversion report.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CVTRPGSRC/SECLVL'.Include second level text (SECLVL)
:P.The second-level text of the message&colon. what it means and what to
do.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CVTRPGSRC/INSRTPL'.Insert specification template (INSRTPL)
:P.Whether to insert specification template.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CVTRPGSRC/LOGFILE'.Log file (LOGFILE)
:P.The log file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QRNCVTLG is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CVTRPGSRC/LOGMBR'.Log file member (LOGMBR)
:P.The log file member for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTBNDDIR.Delete Binding Directory (DLTBNDDIR)
:P.Use the Delete Binding Directory (DLTBNDDIR) command to delete one
binding directory or a generic set of them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTBNDDIR/BNDDIR'.Binding directory (BNDDIR)
:P.The binding directories the binder searches for modules and service
programs to resolve imports.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
