:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPMOD.Display Module (DSPMOD)
:P.Use the Display Module (DSPMOD) command to show the attributes,
exports, imports and procedures of a module.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMOD/MODULE'.Module (MODULE)
:P.The modules bound into the program or service program.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMOD/DETAIL'.Detail (DETAIL)
:P.The detail for this command.
:P.Up to 7 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SIZE, *EXPORT, *IMPORT, *PROCLIST, *REFSYSOBJ,
*COPYRIGHT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMOD/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPPGM.Display Program (DSPPGM)
:P.Use the Display Program (DSPPGM) command to show the attributes,
modules and bound service programs of a program.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPGM/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPGM/DETAIL'.Detail (DETAIL)
:P.The detail for this command.
:P.Up to 7 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the module.
:PT.:PK.*SRVPGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the service program.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SIZE, *ACTGRPEXP, *COPYRIGHT, *SIGNATURE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPGM/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPPGMREF.Display Program References (DSPPGMREF)
:P.Use the Display Program References (DSPPGMREF) command to list the
files and objects a program refers to.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPGMREF/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPGMREF/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPGMREF/OBJTYPE'.Object type (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:P.Up to 5 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.Programs.
:PT.:PK.*SQLPKG:EPK.
:PD.SQL packages.
:PT.:PK.*SRVPGM:EPK.
:PD.Service programs.
:PT.:PK.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.Modules.
:PT.:PK.*QRYDFN:EPK.
:PD.Query definitions.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPGMREF/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPGMREF/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPSRVPGM.Display Service Program (DSPSRVPGM)
:P.Use the Display Service Program (DSPSRVPGM) command to show the
attributes, modules, exports and signatures of a service program.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSRVPGM/SRVPGM'.Service program (SRVPGM)
:P.The service program, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSRVPGM/DETAIL'.Detail (DETAIL)
:P.The detail for this command.
:P.Up to 9 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the module.
:PT.:PK.*SRVPGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the service program.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SIZE, *PROCEXP, *DTAEXP, *ACTGRPEXP,
*COPYRIGHT, *SIGNATURE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSRVPGM/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RCLACTGRP.Reclaim Activation Group (RCLACTGRP)
:P.Use the Reclaim Activation Group (RCLACTGRP) command to delete a
named activation group that is no longer on the call stack, or every
eligible one.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCLACTGRP/ACTGRP'.Activation group (ACTGRP)
:P.The activation group the program runs in&colon. a named one, a new
one each call, or the caller's.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ELIGIBLE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCLACTGRP/OPTION'.Reclaim option (OPTION)
:P.The reclaim option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ABNORMAL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RCLRSC.Reclaim Resources (RCLRSC)
:P.Use the Reclaim Resources (RCLRSC) command to free the resources
(open files, storage) left behind by programs that have ended.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCLRSC/LVL'.Level (LVL)
:P.The level for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CALLER:EPK.
:PD.The activation group of the caller.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVBNDDIRE.Remove Binding Directory Entry (RMVBNDDIRE)
:P.Use the Remove Binding Directory Entry (RMVBNDDIRE) command to remove
entries from a binding directory.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVBNDDIRE/BNDDIR'.Binding directory (BNDDIR)
:P.The binding directories the binder searches for modules and service
programs to resolve imports.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVBNDDIRE/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRVPGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the service program.
:PT.:PK.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the module.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RTVCLSRC.Retrieve CL Source (RTVCLSRC)
:P.Use the Retrieve CL Source (RTVCLSRC) command to write the CL source
kept in a program back to a source member or a stream file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVCLSRC/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVCLSRC/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QCLSRC is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVCLSRC/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the program.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVCLSRC/SRCSTMF'.Source stream file (SRCSTMF)
:P.The path of the stream file that holds the source. When it is given,
SRCFILE and SRCMBR are not used.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVCLSRC/MBROPT'.Member option (MBROPT)
:P.What happens to an existing member that receives data&colon. its
records are replaced, or the new records are added after them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=UPDPGM.Update Program (UPDPGM)
:P.Use the Update Program (UPDPGM) command to replace modules of an ILE
program and rebind it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDPGM/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDPGM/MODULE'.Module (MODULE)
:P.The modules bound into the program or service program.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDPGM/RPLLIB'.Library to replace from (RPLLIB)
:P.The library to replace from for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the module.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDPGM/BNDSRVPGM'.Bind service program (BNDSRVPGM)
:P.The service programs bound by reference to the program.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Service program
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Activation
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*DEFER:EPK.
:PD.Later, when it is needed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDPGM/BNDDIR'.Binding directory (BNDDIR)
:P.The binding directories the binder searches for modules and service
programs to resolve imports.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDPGM/ACTGRP'.Activation group (ACTGRP)
:P.The activation group the program runs in&colon. a named one, a new
one each call, or the caller's.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*CALLER:EPK.
:PD.The activation group of the caller.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDPGM/OPTION'.Creation options (OPTION)
:P.The creation options for this command.
:P.Up to 5 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PK.*NOGEN:EPK.
:PD.The object is not created; only the listing is.
:PT.:PK.*WARN:EPK.
:PD.A warning message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NODUPPROC, *DUPPROC, *NODUPVAR, *DUPVAR,
*NOWARN, *RSLVREF, *UNRSLVREF.
:P.When no value is given, *GEN *NODUPPROC *NODUPVAR *WARN *RSLVREF is
used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDPGM/DETAIL'.Listing detail (DETAIL)
:P.The listing detail for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*EXTENDED:EPK.
:PD.Extended detail.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDPGM/ALWUPD'.Allow update (ALWUPD)
:P.Whether records can be updated through this file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDPGM/ALWLIBUPD'.Allow bound *SRVPGM lib update (ALWLIBUPD)
:P.Whether UPDPGM and UPDSRVPGM may change the library of a bound
service program.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDPGM/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDPGM/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDPGM/ALWRINZ'.Allow reinitialization (ALWRINZ)
:P.Whether the program's static storage may be reinitialized while it is
active.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDPGM/ARGOPT'.Argument optimization (ARGOPT)
:P.Whether argument passing is optimized for the program's procedure
calls.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=UPDSRVPGM.Update Service Program (UPDSRVPGM)
:P.Use the Update Service Program (UPDSRVPGM) command to replace modules
of a service program and rebind it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/SRVPGM'.Service program (SRVPGM)
:P.The service program, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/MODULE'.Module (MODULE)
:P.The modules bound into the program or service program.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/RPLLIB'.Library to replace from (RPLLIB)
:P.The library to replace from for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the module.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/EXPORT'.Export (EXPORT)
:P.The export for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*SRCFILE:EPK.
:PD.The source file of the object.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/SRCFILE'.Export source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QSRVSRC is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/SRCMBR'.Export source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRVPGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the service program.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/SRCSTMF'.Export source stream file (SRCSTMF)
:P.The path of the stream file that holds the source. When it is given,
SRCFILE and SRCMBR are not used.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/BNDSRVPGM'.Bind service program (BNDSRVPGM)
:P.The service programs bound by reference to the program.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Service program
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Activation
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*DEFER:EPK.
:PD.Later, when it is needed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/BNDDIR'.Binding directory (BNDDIR)
:P.The binding directories the binder searches for modules and service
programs to resolve imports.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/ACTGRP'.Activation group (ACTGRP)
:P.The activation group the program runs in&colon. a named one, a new
one each call, or the caller's.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*CALLER:EPK.
:PD.The activation group of the caller.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/OPTION'.Creation options (OPTION)
:P.The creation options for this command.
:P.Up to 5 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PK.*NOGEN:EPK.
:PD.The object is not created; only the listing is.
:PT.:PK.*WARN:EPK.
:PD.A warning message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NODUPPROC, *DUPPROC, *NODUPVAR, *DUPVAR,
*NOWARN, *RSLVREF, *UNRSLVREF.
:P.When no value is given, *GEN *NODUPPROC *NODUPVAR *WARN *RSLVREF is
used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/DETAIL'.Listing detail (DETAIL)
:P.The listing detail for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*EXTENDED:EPK.
:PD.Extended detail.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/ALWUPD'.Allow update (ALWUPD)
:P.Whether records can be updated through this file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/ALWLIBUPD'.Allow bound *SRVPGM lib update (ALWLIBUPD)
:P.Whether UPDPGM and UPDSRVPGM may change the library of a bound
service program.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/ALWRINZ'.Allow reinitialization (ALWRINZ)
:P.Whether the program's static storage may be reinitialized while it is
active.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UPDSRVPGM/ARGOPT'.Argument optimization (ARGOPT)
:P.Whether argument passing is optimized for the program's procedure
calls.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKBNDDIR.Work with Binding Directories (WRKBNDDIR)
:P.Use the Work with Binding Directories (WRKBNDDIR) command to work
with a list of binding directories.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKBNDDIR/BNDDIR'.Binding directory (BNDDIR)
:P.The binding directories the binder searches for modules and service
programs to resolve imports.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
